sequenceDiagram

actor Caller as Customer or administrator
participant Server as server.js
participant Route as routes/bookings.js + guards + validation
participant C as controllers/bookings.js
participant S as services/bookings.js
participant M as Provider / User / Vehicle / Booking
participant DB as MongoDB
Caller->>Server: DELETE /api/v1/bookings/{bookingId}
Server->>Route: Parse and route request
Route->>C: Authenticated authorized actor and validated bookingId
C->>S: cancelBooking(id, actor, now)
activate S
S->>M: Read scoped booking references
M->>DB: Ownership-scoped reference lookup
S->>DB: Start transaction
S->>M: Guard provider, user, then vehicle
M->>DB: Increment revisions sequentially in same session
S->>M: Re-read scoped booking
M->>DB: Read current state/dates
alt Already cancelled
    Note over S,DB: No additional cancellation write
else Cancellation permitted
    S->>M: Set cancelled state, actor, time and role-based reason
    M->>DB: Save in same session
else Completed, or customer at/after start
    break Cancellation rejected
        S->>DB: Abort
        S-->>C: Throw AppError 409
        C-->>Server: next(error)
        Server-->>Caller: 409 safe JSON error
    end
end
Note over S,DB: Commit only on successful branches, thrown failures leave through shared error handler
DB-->>S: Commit on success
S->>M: Populate selected customer contact after commit
M->>DB: Read current contact
S-->>C: Booking
deactivate S
C->>C: Serialize retained booking and derived cancelled status
C-->>Server: 200 JSON on success
Server-->>Caller: Success JSON or safe error
